      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is highly dependent on the model and its rig and isn't a bug. For example, none of my avatars have this issue and I haven't performed the adjustment described below.\nYou can adjust the range that you permit finger spread in the muscle configuration page in Unity. Click on your model in your project (usually your FBX), go to the Rigging tab, click Configure, and go to the muscles & settings tab in your inspector.\nThere, you can go to your fingers and adjust the spread settings. You'll have a range you can adjust. Slide that range around and you can adjust how it looks.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
